From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maxim Stepanov <g.maxim.stepanoff@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 5 Jul 2026 01:16:56 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] database_client: fix results grid rendering no rows (definite
 height for grid in value-viewer row)

The value-viewer split wrapped the results area in an h_flex row. There
.flex_1() governs width, not height, so the grid lost a definite-height
ancestor. ui::Table's uniform_list uses ListSizingBehavior::Auto (fills
its flex parent rather than measuring content), so with an indefinite
height it collapsed to the header's min-content: the header rendered but
zero data rows laid out. Give the grid-bearing results_area branches
.h_full() (mirroring the value-viewer panel, which already had it) plus
.min_w_0() so the split shrinks correctly.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018Rpitr6Ztn5nr3BMaHvESX
---
 crates/database_client/src/query_view.rs | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/database_client/src/query_view.rs b/crates/database_client/src/query_view.rs
index ef20ad9b3d..496bf7be26 100644
--- a/crates/database_client/src/query_view.rs
+++ b/crates/database_client/src/query_view.rs
@@ -1964,12 +1964,15 @@ impl Render for QueryView {
                 v_flex()
                     .flex_1()
                     .w_full()
+                    .h_full()
+                    .min_w_0()
                     .min_h_0()
                     .child(banner)
                     .child(
                         div()
                             .flex_1()
                             .w_full()
+                            .min_h_0()
                             .overflow_hidden()
                             .child(self.results_grid.clone()),
                     )
@@ -1999,6 +2002,9 @@ impl Render for QueryView {
                 div()
                     .flex_1()
                     .w_full()
+                    .h_full()
+                    .min_w_0()
+                    .min_h_0()
                     .overflow_hidden()
                     .child(self.results_grid.clone())
                     .into_any_element()
